@startuml control-pid-library
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam componentStyle uml2
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 45
skinparam ranksep 35

title truST Control PID Library: Public Surface And Conformance Flow

package "Normative Inputs" {
  artifact "Control PID Specification\ndocs/specs/45-control-pid.md" as spec
  artifact "Paper Listings 3-5\nand released examples" as paper
}

package "Reusable Control Package\nlibraries/control" {
  component "Control.PID\ncombined positional/incremental state" as pid
  component "Control.LowPass\nindependent one/two-stage state" as filter
  component "Parameter, input, and\ninitial-state records" as records
  component "Mode, anti-windup, and\nfilter-order enums" as enums
}

package "Native ST Conformance Fixture" {
  component "Equation oracles\nSections 7.1-7.12" as equations
  component "Seven released scenarios\nSection 7.13" as scenarios
  component "trust-dev ST test runner" as runner
}

package "Actual PID applications" {
  component "Primary commissioning example\ncomplete parameter record + startup state\nManual / Auto + fixed 100 ms simulation" as commissioning
  component "Heater P / PI lessons\nwindup and response trials\nactivation and input checks" as lessons
  component "Manual PI tuning lesson\nreview one bounded record leaf\nreapply after explicit trial reset" as manual_tuning
  component "Heater diagnosis lesson\nmeasured / unbiased reference inputs\npaired request and applied feedback" as diagnosis
  component "Read-only GetState snapshot\ncopy of seven retained histories\npost anti-windup nominal output" as observation
  component "Ordinary PLC output / input\nactuator -> process -> sensor" as plant_io
}

spec --> pid
spec --> filter
paper --> spec : baseline source
records --> pid : complete samples and state
records --> filter : filter parameters
enums --> pid : mode and anti-windup selection
enums --> filter : order selection
equations --> pid
equations --> filter
scenarios --> pid
scenarios --> filter
runner --> equations : compiles and executes
runner --> scenarios : compiles and executes
commissioning --> pid : Configure / Initialize / Update
lessons --> pid : existing controller owns output
manual_tuning --> records : task-boundary parameter apply / rollback
manual_tuning --> pid : retain full accepted record and state
diagnosis --> pid : same Configure / Initialize / Update
pid --> plant_io : limited output
plant_io --> commissioning : measured PV
plant_io --> lessons : measured PV
plant_io --> manual_tuning : measured PV / applied heater input
plant_io --> diagnosis : native measured/reference channels + applied input
pid --> observation : value copy; no update
observation --> lessons : truthful state diagnostics
observation --> diagnosis : unlimited request; no parallel controller

note left of plant_io
The setpoint/load heater trials reuse one
native state-space plant: delayed heating,
immediate extraction, one measured PV.
ST does not sum separate plant responses.
Diagnosis publishes an unbiased reference from
the same native state; a channel-0 sensor-bias
event affects only the measured input.
end note

note right of pid
One state owner implements the paper's
exact IntegralGain = 0 form switch.
There are no duplicate P, PI, PD,
or PID state machines.
end note

note right of filter
Filtering remains caller-owned and
uses a separate instance per signal.
The controller has no hidden filter.
end note

note bottom of scenarios
Python and MATLAB are reference sources only.
Native conformance executes Structured Text.
end note

@enduml
